  "findings": [
    "Expanded collector captures all 52 native threads at both late snapshots in about 80ms. Main CPU runtime increases while all ten workers remain asleep with unchanged runtime.",
    "Both observed job queues have null heads and tails and five sleeping workers. The workers have zero wake credits and no deferred wakes; their associated mutexes have no owner. The movie decoder and I/O worker also wait on unowned mutex/condition contexts. These observations do not support a worker mutex deadlock, but cannot rule out earlier failures.",
    "The main thread walks job records, helps the selected queue, and spins when no runnable work is found. The value at group+4 is a job count, not a completion counter expected to reach zero. Its first job state remains 0; the wait skips state 2. Group state remains 1, whereas captured queue code writes 2 before enqueueing and 3 when the last job is taken. This suggests the group was never published; the producer path is not yet captured, so this remains an inference.",
    "GpuComm stack context matches Liverpool::Process waiting for commands/submits. All live performance counters are unchanged from 80s to 110s: last submit at 33.234450115s, last draw at 33.201201446s. GpuInterrupt remains in the event wait; no GPU fault is reported. This is not evidence of a long-running current GPU shader.",
    "Late screenshots are byte-identical black output. The 29 FPS overlay does not show game progress. Protected termination at 119.614s requires SIGKILL; it is not a clean game exit. Ollama is restored and the installed binary remains unchanged.",
    "Capture limits omit the wait wrapper at 0xb097c0, portions of enqueue code, and a GPU interrupt pointer table. No emulator defect is sufficiently established for a semantic patch."
  ],
